.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_BEGIN_MPQE 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe \- begin creating an MPQE-wrapped patch archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe("
.BI "        mpq_patch_s **" "patch,"
.BI "        const char *" "base_archive,"
.BI "        const char *" "output_patch,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "auth_code,"
.BI "        size_t " "auth_code_size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a staged MPQE-wrapped patch artifact using an ordinary filesystem MPQ
at \fIbase_archive\fP. The base remains unchanged. The caller supplies the
authentication code used by the existing MPQE container writer; the code need
only remain valid during this call. A matching code is required to read or
apply the finished patch. Patch members retain the ordinary PTCH/COPY/BSD0
semantics. Finish publishes the encrypted artifact; abort discards it. Both
operations consume the patch handle, even on error. On failure, a valid
\fIpatch\fP output is set to NULL. Weak signing can be configured with
libmpq__patch_sign(3); no external strong-signature representation is defined
for MPQE transport. This creation API does not accept embedded or MPQE base
archives.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid arguments, authentication-code errors, unsupported base formats,
allocation failures, and I/O errors may propagate.
